{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109283","id":2716271476,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6h5wN0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109283.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109283/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109283/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109283/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/58766486665f4f508df3c715cb5fbfca1d104794","number":109283,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix C# environment variables access on Linux (SDL-related bug)","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024\r\n\r\nFor some reason, these SDL defines mess with C#'s ability to use environment variables on Linux, I'm not sure why that is happening, but this fix was tested and it should resolve the issue (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109024#issuecomment-3137304522 ).\r\n\r\nThis fix must also be tested on a Steam Deck in case it messes with Steam Deck's built in controls or Steam Input, because otherwise it would be a regression from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108350 (I don't have a Steam Deck, so I can't test it myself :( )\r\n\r\nAnd also, the bug is only reproducible with HAVE_GETENV, HAVE_SETENV and HAVE_UNSETENV defined, and if they're all defined, SDL defines HAVE_LIBC_ENVIRONMENT here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/45509c284cc8779f7e791b0d7dc3d639b3cc2fcc/thirdparty/sdl/stdlib/SDL_getenv.c#L35-L47\r\nI'm not an expert in C# integration in C++ or environment variables, but if someone has an idea on why this piece of code messes with C#, we would like to know!\n\nTODO:\n- [x] Fix Steam Deck controls","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdparty","name":"topic:thirdparty","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by"